iEvqH131g726igADhSrX6As-CnxYI2uvywaPqN4dtp1GUlX-81jDkUyRfAKZSNUanSa57WBG_71-GS4PebZBXw8YEGoRNK12UpXBr_FXwbaaTIShw5NoYpE95V5nK4SF9Q9x1sLjT-AgD8hxrso0g5nbSRaT9LAdzMjrYgboCWaoLUZYFecWg68xvUxMRC5Y1sxd9k8bc-EH33VsWhiKAinl7fSWuZIShlsHZ4j-T6OMIX-NLPGXBraIZrYkR5x-kC0oqWmv5C0S2BIib7yHdol_U-GLAS3UJSKf2e5g0_ml70-NkDDr2eq3pYpfmOc23UwOSq5QqG3g41KJTdhS9SRer_KZms7MR_bGmOhXc-ZFSz0XniSsHcIOD8FgpN-mgt-uxYBLB6cPP8XQoePqpcEE1cDF7bjv37YCI_YfZc3D-AFU8pij-e0OuTIDSW9Xw5L6uAowCt5h0p8TJ3NVeMSuo5NnRyOXFnN-q3To_N1nNjCjVAZsoUGgR8cKCJY840dYeCAlTYKtzHj3x_ipvK1pky1mhTrN4IiH1NK4_Cwz8cpMAHqqnjHBUhOG2io2FMJtRJ8p-Bn7h7YVhEy0mr-ecK_6j_wt_ehKUkiJYB4sfKqkSSTCtN8awUUckWD58Z_grJ4V0d8oViIBk9L3cWxpgy6YDewRWmFCzr5_kjmLBNj4tXibYApP9yCpdCplLr7JQ1IRt5dJ5oYRxPlUT9RaC7q69mYsatArFuFYDQplSjPAaolAAalzjUuyfI64oaFBUFxb4u1nX749E70SEKzfSxHA5ApGaK9_0IOcmaKPQ-EV6V-5rlbhk8WF-DeLKlPBXpKBHeEoW1MRlqfjdS334t-sRDxjbIj3hQKiDOFGBmpQH67S8UendHrR98DtkKrbqKHGn_bWhDLPKsf2U3d6_ju0ExS7uB1hF1_9xASaufEVjr2gWugRPS7ljHgXa4zFl1ZtMu442VT6ANaNgT4wpnclH29toqqexHBrgUJZxBLkYF4KVmegklgYGzKsq-lFQdf1nb6qhKkhPrMHTz1WO"},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_041ba8b48e51d02f016adb42b364e48191815c22caa5bb1001","call_id":"call_84e82ac7830a4c6cb984e2f211206328","name":"submit_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"base_input\":\"prior-candidate.json\",\"patches\":[{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/0/text\",\"value\":\"Let D=dim_H(E) and let F=E×[0,1] with the stipulated concatenated Euclidean metric. First, 0≤D≤n<∞: for n=0 the ambient space is a singleton. For n>0, compactness gives a bounded box containing E; cover that box by a grid of cubes of side h. For 0<h≤1 the number is at most C h^(−n), for a constant C depending only on the box and n, each cube has Euclidean diameter at most √n h, and for every real m>n their total m-power diameter cost is at most C(√n)^m h^(m−n), tending to zero. The definition of Hausdorff dimension as the critical exponent therefore gives D≤n. In particular D is a finite real number and all subsequent choices of exponents are legitimate. For the upper bound, fix any real q>D. Since D≥0, q>0. The threshold definition of Hausdorff dimension gives H^q(E)=0. Here, explicitly, the scale-δ content is the infimum over Nat-indexed sequences (U_j) with E⊆⋃j U_j and diam(U_j)≤δ of the extended nonnegative sum Σ'j diam(U_j)^q; the Hausdorff measure is the increasing-small-scale limit of these contents (the pinned convention has no normalization factor). Thus for each δ>0 and each ζ>0 there is such a cover with total q-cost below ζ. Empty sets may be removed. At n=0, F is isometric to [0,1], so its dimension is 1 and the theorem follows directly; this branch is taken before any positive-diameter replacement. Hence suppose n>0. For any zero-diameter nonempty member U_j choose a point u_j∈U_j and replace U_j by an open Euclidean ball centered at u_j with positive diameter r_j≤δ; choose the radii so their q-costs sum to less than any prescribed additional ζ (for countably many indices, assign the j-th replacement cost <ζ2^(−j)). Keep positive-diameter members, and write r_j for their diameters; the resulting cover has 0<r_j≤δ and arbitrarily small Σj r_j^q. Take δ≤1. Partition [0,1] into at most 1/r_j+1 closed intervals of lengths at most r_j. Their products with U_j cover U_j×[0,1]. In the concatenated metric, squared distance is the sum of squared coordinate distances, so diam(U_j×K)≤√(r_j²+r_j²)=√2 r_j. Consequently the total (q+1)-power cost of all these product sets is bounded by Σj(1/r_j+1)(√2 r_j)^(q+1)≤2(√2)^(q+1)Σj r_j^q, since r_j≤1. Their diameters are ≤√2δ. As the original q-cost and replacement cost can be made arbitrarily small, the (q+1)-dimensional Hausdorff measure of F is zero. The dimension threshold implication gives dim_H(F)≤q+1. This holds for every q>D, and taking the infimum over q>D yields dim_H(F)≤D+1.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/text\",\"value\":\"For the lower bound when D>0, fix a real s with 0<s<D. Let C_a(A,δ) denote exactly the infimum of Σ'i (ediam U_i)^a over Nat-indexed covers (U_i) of A with ediam(U_i)≤δ for all i. Here ediam takes values in ENNReal, and a>0 is interpreted through its NNReal/ENNReal coercions; 0^a=0. From the pinned formula for Hausdorff measure, H^a(A)=sup_{δ>0} C_a(A,δ)=lim_{δ↓0}C_a(A,δ): both use the same Nat-indexed cover sequences, the same ediam diameter cutoff, and the same tsum, and the formula's supremum over nonempty-member witnesses contributes the term ediam(U_i)^a for nonempty U_i and zero for empty U_i, equal to that term since ediam(∅)=0. For δ1≤δ2, the admissible δ1 covers are a subset of the δ2 covers, so C_a(A,δ1)≥C_a(A,δ2); hence the decreasing-scale limit equals the supremum over positive δ. The dimension threshold theorem applied at NNReal exponent s says H^s(E)=∞ because (s:ENNReal)<dim_H(E). Therefore C_s(E,δ) tends to ∞ as δ decreases to zero. Fix 0<δ≤1 and an arbitrary Nat-indexed δ-cover (V_i) of F; discard empty members and put ρ_i=ediam(V_i)≤δ. Let A_i and B_i be its coordinate projections. The coordinate projections are 1-Lipschitz for the concatenated metric, so ediam(A_i),ediam(B_i)≤ρ_i. Choose η_i=ε·2^(−(i+1))/(1+ρ_i^s)>0, so Σ'i η_iρ_i^s≤ε, and choose an open interval J_i containing B_i with length at most ρ_i+η_i. Such an interval exists because B_i is bounded (its diameter is at most finite ρ_i); take an interval extending each side of its infimum/supremum by a total additional width no more than η_i. For every t∈[0,1], the A_i with t∈J_i cover E: if x∈E then (x,t) lies in some V_i; thus x∈A_i and t∈B_i⊆J_i. Each A_i has diameter ≤δ, so the definition of C_s gives pointwise C_s(E,δ)≤Σ'i 1_{J_i∩[0,1]}(t)ρ_i^s. Each summand is a nonnegative ENNReal-valued measurable function on [0,1] with restricted Lebesgue measure, since J_i∩[0,1] is Borel. Integrate this pointwise inequality: monotonicity of the ENNReal lintegral gives C_s(E,δ)≤∫⁻_{[0,1]} Σ'i 1_{J_i∩[0,1]}ρ_i^s. Countable Tonelli, applied to these AEMeasurable summands, identifies the integral with Σ'i ∫⁻ 1_{J_i∩[0,1]}ρ_i^s. The integral of each indicator is the measure of J_i∩[0,1], namely its interval length clipped to [0,1], and is at most ρ_i+η_i; the restricted Lebesgue measure of [0,1] is one. Thus C_s(E,δ)≤Σ'i(ρ_i+η_i)ρ_i^s≤Σ'iρ_i^(s+1)+ε. Terms with ρ_i=0 vanish because s>0. Since ε>0 was arbitrary, C_s(E,δ)≤Σ'iρ_i^(s+1) for every chosen cover V_i. Taking the infimum over all such covers gives C_s(E,δ)≤C_(s+1)(F,δ). As δ↓0 the left side tends to infinity, so the right side does also; the exact scale-content formula then gives H^(s+1)(F)=∞. The dimension threshold implication in the reverse direction yields s+1≤dim_H(F). This holds for every 0<s<D; taking the supremum over those s proves D+1≤dim_H(F). All scalar use of the threshold results is at NNReal exponents: s is represented by its NNReal coercion and the measure formula uses the corresponding real coercion, with no identification of distinct scalar types suppressed.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/2/text\",\"value\":\"If D=0, choose x₀∈E by H001. Define p:F→[0,1] by p(x,t)=t. Since |t−u|≤((|x−y|²+|t−u|²))^(1/2), p is 1-Lipschitz. It is onto because p(x₀,t)=t for every t∈[0,1]. Apply the general Lipschitz image dimension inequality to p and the set F: dim_H([0,1])=dim_H(p(F))≤dim_H(F). The interval dimension is 1: [0,1] has nonempty interior in the one-dimensional real vector space, so the pinned theorem Real.dimH_of_nonempty_interior gives dimension finrank_R(R)=1. Therefore dim_H(F)≥1=D+1. This branch includes n=0, but the direct n=0 isometry branch in S001 already handled the upper bound without any positive-diameter replacement. Combining this lower bound when D=0, the slicing lower bound when D>0, and the upper bound for all D proves dim_H(F)=dim_H(E)+1.\"}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and mathematical grounds. SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT stops for a real source-access/original-input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished drafting, source registration or format work must use TASK_INCOMPLETE: this records progress without ending the stage; continue the actual work. Difficulty or artifact incompletion alone is not a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"obstacle_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["obstacle_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration","module"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible; choose a narrow pointer for large objects.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"}},"required":["candidate","pointer"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"5cdf806c-9a5a-48a8-bb64-9ccc84c5e8d6","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"low"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"high","context":"all_turns","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":52699,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":39936,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2241,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":197},"total_tokens":54940,"attribution":{"items":{"fc_041ba8b48e51d02f016adb4216fe7081919de373a1cb4b11d7":{"input_tokens":31,"cached_tokens":31,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_041ba8b48e51d02f016adb4218e71c8191b81ae50307c49126":{"input_tokens":34,"cached_tokens":34,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_041ba8b48e51d02f016adb421b24408191b747ba9b483d08c5":{"input_tokens":34,"cached_tokens":34,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_041ba8b48e51d02f016adb421d93e48191813b4b946473c7fa":{"input_tokens":33,"cached_tokens":33,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_041ba8b48e51d02f016adb422011808191bcf3dde48a941be0":{"input_tokens":35,"cached_tokens":35,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_041ba8b48e51d02f016adb4222f5bc81918a87f5f7a0a98435":{"input_tokens":34,"cached_tokens":34,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_041ba8b48e51d02f016adb42255f048191922fe730738ca5d7":{"input_tokens":33,"cached_tokens":33,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_041ba8b48e51d02f016adb4227b0388191af615cbd19ba45b8":{"input_tokens":35,"cached_tokens":35,"cache_write_tokens":0,